# TaskFlow

TaskFlow is a polished, responsive team task management website. This GitHub-ready version is a standalone static site: its HTML, CSS, and JavaScript are bundled in `index.html`, with no build step or package installation required.

## Features

- Dashboard with live task totals, workflow distribution, upcoming work, and activity visualization
- Create, edit, complete, search, filter, and delete tasks
- Drag-and-drop Kanban board with To do, In progress, In review, and Completed columns
- Create and remove projects; view project task progress
- Calendar with month navigation and clickable task details
- Team directory and an in-app invitation link alternative
- Light and dark themes, responsive mobile navigation, confirmation prompts, and feedback messages
- Browser local storage so tasks and projects persist after refresh on the same device

## Open the website

Download or clone this folder, then open `index.html` in Chrome, Edge, Firefox, or another modern browser. You can also use GitHub Pages: publish the repository and set Pages to deploy from the branch and folder containing `index.html`.

No npm, server, database, external image files, or local asset paths are required. Google Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts when an internet connection is available; the browser uses its fallback fonts if they cannot load.

## Data and privacy

This standalone edition stores tasks, projects, and the theme preference in the current browser's local storage. Data does not sync between devices or team members. Use **Settings → Clear all local data** to remove the saved workspace from this browser.

